    <statement><p>The expression <m>\displaystyle{\ \sqrt{x^5 y^2} \sqrt[3]{x^5 y^3} \sqrt[5]{x^4} \ }</m> equals <m>\displaystyle{\ x^ry^s \ }</m></p>
<p>where <m>\ r</m>, the exponent of <m>\ x</m>, is: <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>and <m>\ s</m>, the exponent of <m>\ y</m>, is: <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{5}{2}}+{\frac{5}{3}}+{\frac{4}{5}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{gathered} \sqrt{x^5 y^2} \sqrt[3]{x^5 y^3}\sqrt[5]{x^4} = 
(x^5 y^2)^{1/2} (x^5 y^3)^{1/3} (x^4)^{1/5}  \\
=   x^{5/2} y^{2/2} x^{5/3} y^{3/3} x^{4/5}
= x^{(5/2+5/3+4/5)} y^{(2/2+3/3)} \\
=  x^{149/30} y^{2/1}. \end{gathered} }</m></p>
<p>Therefore <m>r = {{\frac{149}{30}}}</m> and <m>s={2}</m>.</p>
</solution>
